Autoconf sources for tbaMUD
===========================

  configure.ac   what autoconf reads
  aclocal.m4     tbaMUD's own macros: AC_CHECK_PROTO and AC_UNSAFE_CRYPT

The 'configure' script at the top of the tree and 'src/conf.h.in' are both
generated from these two files.  Do not edit either one by hand.  The next
regeneration discards the edit without saying so, which is how the tree
ended up carrying a 'configure' that no longer matched its own source.

To regenerate, run both of these from the top of the tree -- not from here:

  autoconf   -I cnf -o configure cnf/configure.ac
  autoheader -I cnf              cnf/configure.ac

Commit 'configure' and 'src/conf.h.in' along with whatever you changed.
Both are tracked so that people building the mud do not need autoconf.

Requires autoconf 2.69 or newer; 2.72 generated the files in the tree now.

One file autoheader does not write
----------------------------------

'src/conf.h.cmake.in' holds the same symbols for the CMake build, which
configures it instead of 'src/conf.h.in'.  Nothing generates it and nothing
checks it against this directory, so it only stays in step by hand.  Add an
AC_DEFINE that anything under src/ reads and you have to add it there too,
or the CMake build compiles without it and says nothing.

The two agree as things stand.  'src/conf.h.cmake.in' is short only the ten
symbols autoconf emits of its own accord -- the six PACKAGE_* and
HAVE_STDIO_H, HAVE_STDLIB_H, HAVE_STDINT_H, HAVE_INTTYPES_H -- and no tbaMUD
source reads any of them.
